{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Sows</b> — if the rich man acts unjustly to rule over the poor, he shall reap trouble; he shall receive his due recompense." "<b>And the rod</b> — for outrage is likened to a rod, as in: 'Assyria, the rod of my anger' (Isaiah 10:5). The meaning: he who perpetrates outrage against the poor — the rod shall perish and shall no longer pass through them, for HaShem shall destroy it."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:09.151983438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}